From c5143238b49d8ba9c60ae32f553eb3ffca3f870d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <huhuvmb88@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 23:24:54 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: ROCKET_B_VALUE to force the weight zero point
 correction

A constant input at exactly in_zp makes every MAC product zero, so the output
must be requant(bias), and cropping conv2d-cal's kernel leaves its bias and its
requant untouched. On hardware the answer still depends on the kernel size: 12
distinct values at 5x5, 45 at 1x1, and a flat zero point at 3x3.

B is the only k-dependent term in that path. It carries the difference between
the MAC's sum((in - 0x80)(w - 0x80)) and the true sum((in - in_zp)(w - wt_zp)),
which is proportional to the input sum over the kernel window and so to the tap
count.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
index 6840a6d..4ccd001 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_coefs.c
@@ -590,7 +590,26 @@ rkt_fill_biases(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
                uint32_t av = (uint32_t)strtoul(getenv("ROCKET_DW_ATEST"), NULL, 0);
                *A = (av > 1) ? (int32_t)av : 0x2000;
             }
-            *B = (int16_t)(0x80 - (int)wt_zp);
+            /*
+             * ROCKET_B_VALUE: force the wt_zp correction operand. The hardware
+             * MAC computes sum((in - 0x80) * (w - 0x80)) while the true conv is
+             * sum((in - in_zp) * (w - wt_zp)), and B carries the difference,
+             * which is proportional to the input sum over the kernel window and
+             * therefore to the TAP COUNT: 400 taps at 5x5, 144 at 3x3, 16 at
+             * 1x1.
+             *
+             * That matters because a constant input at exactly in_zp makes
+             * (in - 0x80) zero, so the MAC is zero by construction and the
+             * output has to be requant(bias), identical for every kernel size,
+             * since cropping conv2d-cal's kernel leaves its bias and its
+             * requant untouched. On hardware it is not identical: the baseline
+             * comes back with 12 distinct values at 5x5, 45 at 1x1, and a flat
+             * zero point at 3x3. Something k-dependent is being added to a MAC
+             * that should be zero, and B is the only k-dependent term.
+             */
+            *B = getenv("ROCKET_B_VALUE")
+                    ? (int16_t)strtol(getenv("ROCKET_B_VALUE"), NULL, 0)
+                    : (int16_t)(0x80 - (int)wt_zp);
             /*
              * C is a Q14 per-channel scale ratio (=0x4000 for the max-scale channel).
              * If the HW does NOT apply a built-in >>14 after the BS C-multiply, this
-- 
